From 6342ab970ee894201ef307ebda826b0445ceddf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-ID: <6342ab970ee894201ef307ebda826b0445ceddf1.1791283768.git.ben.grande.b@gmail.com>
From: Ben Grande <ben.grande.b@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:22:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH libvirt] libxl: Fire reboot event

Fired on "on_reboot" values "restart" and "destroy", so event listeners
can react to this request. The value "destroy" is useful for
applications that have routines run between restarts, therefore the
reboot event is still fired in this case. If the value is set to
"preserve" then it doesn't seem appropriate to fire reboot event.

Resolves: https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues/8196
Signed-off-by: Ben Grande <ben.grande.b@gmail.com>
---
 docs/formatdomain.rst    | 14 +++++++++++---
 src/libvirt-domain.c     |  4 +++-
 src/libxl/libxl_domain.c |  4 ++++
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/formatdomain.rst b/docs/formatdomain.rst
index e4eb2d9..a5388c5 100644
--- a/docs/formatdomain.rst
+++ b/docs/formatdomain.rst
@@ -2047,9 +2047,17 @@ Each of these states allow for the same four possible actions.
    The domain will be terminated and then restarted with a new name. (Only
    supported by the libxl hypervisor driver.)
 
-QEMU/KVM/HVF supports the ``on_poweroff`` and ``on_reboot`` events handling the
-``destroy`` and ``restart`` actions, but the combination of ``on_poweroff`` set
-to ``restart`` and ``on_reboot`` set to ``destroy`` is forbidden.
+QEMU/KVM/HVF/XEN supports the ``on_poweroff`` and ``on_reboot`` events handling
+the ``destroy`` and ``restart`` actions, in which case, a notification is
+available when the reboot fires, using the event ID
+``VIR_DOMAIN_EVENT_ID_REBOOT``.
+
+Setting ``on_reboot`` to ``destroy``, prevents libvirt from restarting the
+domain on its own, thus allowing a VMM that monitors
+``VIR_DOMAIN_EVENT_ID_REBOOT``, to run their own stop and start procedures.
+
+The combination of ``on_poweroff`` set to ``restart`` and ``on_reboot`` set to
+``destroy`` is forbidden.
 
 The ``on_crash`` event supports these additional actions :since:`since 0.8.4`.
 
diff --git a/src/libvirt-domain.c b/src/libvirt-domain.c
index acd9ffc..95764eb 100644
--- a/src/libvirt-domain.c
+++ b/src/libvirt-domain.c
@@ -1779,7 +1779,9 @@ virDomainShutdownFlags(virDomainPtr domain, unsigned int flags)
  * Note that the guest OS may ignore the request.
  * Additionally, the hypervisor may check and support the domain
  * 'on_reboot' XML setting resulting in a domain that shuts down instead
- * of rebooting.
+ * of rebooting. Depending on the hypervisor and 'on_reboot' setting,
+ * VIR_DOMAIN_EVENT_ID_REBOOT might be emitted. For more information, see
+ * https://libvirt.org/formatdomain.html#events-configuration
  *
  * If @flags is set to zero, then the hypervisor will choose the
  * method of shutdown it considers best. To have greater control
diff --git a/src/libxl/libxl_domain.c b/src/libxl/libxl_domain.c
index 51dc3ed..8163604 100644
--- a/src/libxl/libxl_domain.c
+++ b/src/libxl/libxl_domain.c
@@ -550,10 +550,14 @@ libxlDomainShutdownThread(void *opaque)
                                            VIR_DOMAIN_EVENT_STOPPED_SHUTDOWN);
         switch ((virDomainLifecycleAction) vm->def->onReboot) {
         case VIR_DOMAIN_LIFECYCLE_ACTION_DESTROY:
+            virObjectEventStateQueue(driver->domainEventState,
+                                            virDomainEventRebootNewFromObj(vm));
             libxlDomainShutdownHandleDestroy(driver, vm);
             goto endjob;
         case VIR_DOMAIN_LIFECYCLE_ACTION_RESTART:
         case VIR_DOMAIN_LIFECYCLE_ACTION_RESTART_RENAME:
+            virObjectEventStateQueue(driver->domainEventState,
+                                            virDomainEventRebootNewFromObj(vm));
             libxlDomainShutdownHandleRestart(driver, vm);
             goto endjob;
         case VIR_DOMAIN_LIFECYCLE_ACTION_PRESERVE:
